From 9d640bcd5d3261a7474d3e361560265ac3435bbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ljm-233 <2836583630@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:11:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] screencasting: make the frame rate and SHM buffer bound
 configurable

The 30 Hz rate and 32 buffer pool were the values that happened to stop
Electron clients from exhausting memory, but they were compiled in. Expose
them as a `screencasting { }` config block so a user can trade CPU for
smoothness without rebuilding.

Range is 30-120 Hz and 8-256 buffers; values outside that are clamped
rather than rejected, so a typo cannot make the compositor advertise a
rate that stalls the machine.
